Why Fabs Restore Monitor and Qualification Wafers
Test and dummy wafers are needed for chamber conditioning, equipment setup and certain measurement procedures even when no saleable device is being fabricated. High-volume fabs may use substantial quantities in these roles. A qualified reclamation loop can lower material expenditure when the reclaimed surface remains suitable for the intended process.

Recovery requires selective film stripping, controlled polishing, high-purity cleaning and renewed inspection. The wafer becomes thinner during some cycles, while cracks, particles or metallic contamination can restrict further reuse. A reclamation vendor therefore competes on accepted quality and return logistics, not simply the percentage of wafers collected.

